TRADING AND THIRD-PARTY DATA NOTICE
-----------------------------------
Mazkiplay Trade is an analysis and education application, not financial advice.
Trading involves substantial risk. Users remain responsible for every decision,
order, credential, and account. The application does not guarantee profit,
zero-delay data, uninterrupted availability, or the accuracy of any signal.

TradingView names, widgets, symbols, exchange data, news, Twelve Data, Yahoo,
CoinGecko, Indodax, broker/exchange services, and other third-party feeds remain
subject to their respective terms, licenses, rate limits, and data plans. The
project does not represent that every provider supplies licensed tick data for
every asset. Provider availability and plan limitations can cause LIVE, STALE,
or OFFLINE states.

BOT AND MESSAGING NOTICE
------------------------
Optional Telegram, WhatsApp Business Cloud API, and Discord integrations are
outbound notification features. The application does not automate personal
WhatsApp accounts, execute trades, read private broker/exchange accounts, or
store private trading keys. Tokens, access tokens, and webhooks must be supplied
by the user and stored only through the Android Keystore-backed vault.

RESPONSIVE CHART AND BRAND NOTICE
---------------------------------
The application includes responsive portrait/landscape chart controls and
technical-analysis presentation. The premium bull/bear launcher artwork is
project branding for Mazkiplay Trade and is not an official logo or endorsement
of any broker, exchange, data provider, or financial institution.

STARTUP AUDIO NOTICE
--------------------
The project-supplied startup soundtrack is packaged as an application asset and
plays automatically once when the application process starts, then ends at EOF.
The platform may still interrupt audio through calls, audio focus, Bluetooth,
or other system behavior.

TWELVE DATA CREDENTIAL NOTICE
-----------------------------
Twelve Data integration is optional market-data functionality. API credentials
must be entered by the user in the application and are stored using the Android
Keystore-backed vault. No user API key is embedded in source, Git history,
README files, or release binaries. Users are responsible for revoking and
rotating credentials that have been exposed in messages, logs, screenshots, or
other public locations.

ONLINE-ONLY NOTICE
------------------
The application may require a validated internet connection and can block the
main UI when connectivity is unavailable. This is an application behavior, not
a guarantee that every provider endpoint is online or realtime.
